# Cloudflare Pages headers. The CSP allows only this origin and the kit.
# atproto is the exception, and here is exactly why: a learner signs in at their own PDS, whose host is
# whatever they chose. public.api.bsky.app resolves handles, plc.directory resolves did:plc, but the
# token endpoint and every repo call go to a domain this app cannot know in advance. So connect-src
# admits https endpoints, while script-src, form-action and base-uri stay shut - which is where the
# exfiltration routes actually are. Narrowing this further means running the OAuth client inside the
# service worker, where page CSP does not reach: deferred, not overlooked.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://kit.thatsit.app; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://kit.thatsit.app; font-src https://kit.thatsit.app; img-src 'self' data: blob:; connect-src 'self' https://kit.thatsit.app https://plc.directory https://public.api.bsky.app https:; manifest-src 'self'; worker-src 'self'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

# Hashed file names, so they never change. Pages merges matching blocks, so /* still applies here.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
